Restore the AW8736 Mode 3 pulse train on amplifier enable.

The AW8736 latches its gain from the number of rising edges on its enable
pin at power-up. r185 replaced the vendor pulse train with a single level
change, which selects mode 1 - the lowest gain - on every enable.

Measured on Device #1 against stock Device #3, same microphone, same room,
playing the identical volume-adjust earcon: stock -27.0 dBFS, pmOS
-40.7 dBFS, and stock sits further from the microphone so the true gap is
larger. pmOS own level is stable to 0.41 dB over eight plays, so this is
systematic. The EQ curve is byte-identical to stock EQ_50, every MBCL
parameter matches including the full-band limiter, the codec registers
match (PCM 127, HP Driver Gain 6/6), PipeWire sits at 0.00 dB and the
stereo-to-mono sum is correct - none of them account for it.

r185 justified the removal with the vendor aud_pins_extamp_gain0..3
pinctrl states being bound by nothing, so AudDrv_GPIO_EXTAMP_Gain_Set()
fails on every call. That is correct, but it describes MediaTek gain path
on GPIO28/29, not the AW8736 edge counting on its own enable pin.

--- a/sound/soc/mediatek/mt8163/mt8163-biscuit.c
+++ b/sound/soc/mediatek/mt8163/mt8163-biscuit.c
@@ -98,6 +98,37 @@
 		return;
 
 	if (on) {
+		/*
+		 * AW8736 Mode 3.
+		 *
+		 * The part latches its gain from the NUMBER OF RISING EDGES on
+		 * its enable pin during power-up, so a single clean level change
+		 * selects mode 1 - its lowest gain.
+		 *
+		 * r185 removed this pulse train, reasoning that Biscuit takes its
+		 * amplifier gain from hardware because the vendor's
+		 * aud_pins_extamp_gain0..3 pinctrl states are bound by nothing and
+		 * AudDrv_GPIO_EXTAMP_Gain_Set() therefore fails on every call.
+		 * That is true, but it is about MediaTek's own gain path on
+		 * GPIO28/29 - a different mechanism from the AW8736 counting edges
+		 * on its own enable pin, which is a property of the part. One
+		 * being dead says nothing about the other.
+		 *
+		 * Restored because the device measured ~14 dB quieter than stock
+		 * playing an identical asset, with the EQ curve, every MBCL
+		 * parameter, the codec registers, the PipeWire graph and the
+		 * stereo-to-mono sum all verified byte-identical to stock.
+		 */
+		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(priv->speaker_amp, 0);
+		usleep_range(1000, 1200);
+		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(priv->speaker_amp, 1);
+		udelay(2);
+		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(priv->speaker_amp, 0);
+		udelay(2);
+		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(priv->speaker_amp, 1);
+		udelay(2);
+		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(priv->speaker_amp, 0);
+		udelay(2);
 		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(priv->speaker_amp, 1);
 		msleep(MT8163_BISCUIT_AMP_WARMUP_MS);
 	} else {
